<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The DCJ0202 is a type of DC power jack used to provide a reliable connection between an external power supply and an electronic device. It is designed to receive power from a compatible DC plug, typically with an outer diameter of around 2.00 mm, and transfer it to the internal circuitry of the device. DC power jacks like the DCJ0202 are commonly used in small electronic equipment, development boards, and consumer devices where a stable, detachable power connection is needed. The jack usually consists of conductive contacts enclosed in an insulating housing, ensuring both electrical conductivity and mechanical durability. Its design allows easy plugging and unplugging while maintaining a secure fit to prevent accidental disconnection. Depending on the application, it can be mounted on a printed circuit board \(PCB\) using through-hole or surface-mount techniques )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
